WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.660
Clock time is fine,

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:06.120
but psychological time is when future takes over your mind

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.780
and your entire thought patterns are geared only toward future.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:15.180
For many years, before I wrote The Power of Now and it became successful, I was basically a failure.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:19.280
Many people spend their lives in a state of

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.500
almost permanent dissatisfaction.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.540
If you're habitually and frequently unhappy,

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.680
you believe that it has a purpose.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.260
- He's a German-born resident of Canada

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.820
best known as being the author of the book The Power of Now.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.080
In 2008, a New York Times writer called him

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.420
the most popular spiritual author in the United States.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:44.000
His books have sold almost ten million copies across North America.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.620
He's Eckhart Tolle, and here's my take on his top ten rules to success.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:51.180
Rule #1 is my personal favorite, and make sure to stick around all the way to the end

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.600
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.080
Also as Eckhart is talking, if he says something that really resonates with you,

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:58.880
try to copy it down into the comments below and put quotes around it

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.540
so other people can be inspired and learn as well.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.360
So many people have this idea, "I want to achieve something great,

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.480
or be somebody great,"

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:15.220
and they neglect the step that leads to greatness.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.240
They don't honor this step at this moment

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.760
because they have this idea of some future moment where they're going to be great.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:22.600
- Right.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.120
- Some people believe I'm doing great work,

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.080
I mean, I am, because the consciousness is moving through this form.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.160
I don't feel personally responsible for what I do as such.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.440
But even then, it is small steps.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.260
When the writing happens, there's a notepad and a pen,

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.660
and there's the present moment, and there's the stillness. Very small.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:47.400
There's not some idea, "I'm going to create a work that's going to change everybody's consciousness,"

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.460
no, I'm just true to 𝘵𝘩𝘪𝘴 moment, what this moment requires.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:56.080
It's a blank piece of- sheet of paper and a pen,

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:59.260
and the stillness. It's a small thing.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:02.960
It's all a sequence of very small moments.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:06.460
And by being true to this one moment,

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.140
something great arises.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.800
Talking about past and future and excessive emphasis

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.700
on past and future in your life,

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:20.620
yes, of course you need to have... there's nothing wrong with having a certain

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:25.360
intention of what you want to achieve, take steps towards it,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.820
it's part of living here in this dimension.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:31.700
You can't just say "I'm never going to plan anything anymore,"

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.760
just take life as it comes.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.620
Well some people try to do that, but they're not that happy either, after awhile.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.400
(audience laughter)

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.940
So then your life will get very diffused.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:46.940
And so to have an intention, to make a plan; perfectly fine.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:52.000
Either a short-term plan like I'm going to meet you tomorrow at 4 o'clock,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.380
how would you ever meet anybody if we didn't have time? 
(audience laughs)

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:00.080
And future, in a practical level, of course it's needed.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:04.040
The question is whether future takes over your mind.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.520
Being able to use it for practical purposes is, of course, great,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.760
but- I call it- clock time is fine,

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.280
but psychological time is when future takes over your mind

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.200
and your entire thought patterns are geared only toward future,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.860
and you treat the present moment

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:27.040
as either just a means to an end, because it enables you to get to the next one.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:31.960
You're always reaching out, so to speak, internally to the next- you're never quite here,

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.800
always looking for some fulfillment there,

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.920
so you can never embrace the fullness of now,

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.460
or you make the now into even an enemy.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:46.740
Some people are always unhappy- perhaps we all know some- one or two people like that.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.600
- Three.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.380
- (laughter)

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:52.680
- Who are, wherever they are, they're complaining,

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.640
it's never quite right, wherever they are or whoever they are with,

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.300
after a little while, they're very uncomfortable again and should be somewhere else.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.080
You know the bumper sticker that you see on some cars,

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.180
your various versions of it, says "I'd rather be golfing,"

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.540
and then another one says "I'd rather be fishing,"

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:14.040
"I'd rather be this; I'd rather be there."

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:19.260
When I visited the spiritual teacher Ramdas, who lives in Hawaii,

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.440
he has a bumper sticker on--

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:27.180
Ramdas was a person who in the 70's wrote the book "Be Here Now"--

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:31.640
anyway, he has a bumper sticker on his car that says, "I'd rather be here now."

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.400
(laughter)

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.680
So- and then you realize you can actually-

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:44.380
you can still pursue whatever intent where you want to get to a plan,

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:48.220
I call it- it's a bit like a journey, your life is a jouney,

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.700
you're going- you know you want to go from here to there,

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.940
whether you're going to get there, we don't know.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:56.140
Maybe on the way, you'll branch out to somewhere else.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:58.540
But at least you have a certain direction.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:01.620
It's good to have some direction in your life.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:04.760
But while you are travelling,

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:09.160
if your destination takes up most of your attention

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:13.240
and you're continuously focusing on there, you miss all the jouney, really.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:15.260
You can't enjoy the journey anymore.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:17.700
And most of your life 𝘪𝘴 the journey.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:19.920
The arriving is relatively rare.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.220
The wedding, ahhh!

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:25.000
(laughter)

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.780
and a [?] graduation, ahhh!

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:28.740
(laughter)

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:32.260
But so those moments are not the fine view between,

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.240
so the rest is the journey.

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:39.300
And if you can't enjoy the journey, which means the step you're taking at 𝘵𝘩𝘪𝘴 moment

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.580
is really the most important thing.Yes, of course, you know you're going 𝘵𝘩𝘢𝘵 way,

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:46.800
but this step is still to be enjoyed

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:52.100
because that's ultimately- your whole life consists of the step you're taking at this moment.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.740
There is never anything else.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:57.820
For many years, before I wrote The Power of Now and it became successful,

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:01.860
I was basically a failure. (chuckles) In the eyes of the world.

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:05.720
So he's already almost 50, and what has he achieved?

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:08.740
My mom said, "You have thrown away your life.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:11.100
You had so many possibilities in your life.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.680
You walked out of graduate school at Cambridge,

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.300
why did you walk out of there? You..."

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:20.480
My mom and many other people said,

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:24.240
"This person has failed in life. He has no job, he has no...

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:27.340
insurance policies, nothing.
(audience laughs)

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:32.820
No pension plan, just- almost nothing in the bank...

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:34.140
Failure."

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.420
And then a few years later, people bought The Power of Now

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:40.260
and became a bestseller,

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.060
"Oh, a big success!"

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:43.360
Okay,

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:48.960
if I had derived my identity at that time from what the world was telling me,

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.160
or my mind would have told me, if I had been listening to my mind,

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.420
I would have been very unhappy.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:58.100
And I didn't, so I was fine.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:01.660
Because my identity wasn't derived from that anymore.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:07.900
And fortunately, even when, in the eyes of the world, I suddenly became a success,

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.200
I don't want to derive my identity from that.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:14.960
It's just a cheap substitute for who I really am.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:19.100
So I'm not- I don't see- I don't derive--

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:26.060
but the satisfaction that comes is the satisfaction that the work that's happening,

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:29.900
the teaching that's happening, is transforming peoples' lives.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.800
That's very satisfying.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.040
I don't get any personal satisfaction, though, because it's not--

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:38.800
I don't feel it as this separate 'me' produced it.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:43.860
Now it's very easy to mistake an impulse that comes to you

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:49.460
for some deeper answer that comes out of the stillness.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:56.180
And so in any decision-making process, you have basically

00:07:56.180 --> 00:08:01.060
two factors. Well, most people only have...

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:04.500
you have the information that's available to you,

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:11.960
and so make sure that you have the information, all the facts that you need.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:18.380
Sometimes before making a decision, you may have a few- a number of facts,

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:21.880
and sometimes these facts may not be sufficient.

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:28.000
So then you go over them and see what questions you can ask

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:32.180
in order to illicit more facts or information

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:36.880
from whoever is capable of giving to you that information.

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:42.900
I'm talking very general terms, whether you are in business or wherever you are,

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:45.840
or some personal decision that you need to arrive at.

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:51.560
May- on one level, facts are- need to be looked at. What is the situation.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:54.460
And sometimes the facts are not clear enough,

00:08:54.460 --> 00:09:00.540
or there are not enough facts, and you become still and see what questions you can ask,

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:05.940
and somebody may be able to supply more detailed facts.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:09.920
But in order to ask the right question,

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.340
you already need a moment of stillness.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:15.240
So you may not immediately get an answer through stillness.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:18.760
The first step as you become alert and still

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:21.760
is another question.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:25.300
A very important thing in decision-making process

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:30.480
is not to come up with a decision, but to ask the right question

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:35.300
that can illicit what you need in order to arrive at a decision.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.880
And in order to ask the right question,

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:41.480
there needs to be that alert stillness for a moment,

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:46.160
and in that alert stillness, you kind of listen within,

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.540
and then a question comes. This is- I often,

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:54.360
when somebody, like, call me and say, "We've had this or that offer,

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:58.220
somebody wants you to do this, somebody wants you to do that interview,

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:00.220
somebody wants to do that,"

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:04.420
and very often, I don't immediately say yes or no.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:07.200
I usually come up with a few questions

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:11.080
what-- in addition to the information that they gave me,

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:16.800
well, what about that and that and that, and then say, "Oh okay, I'll get back to you. I'll find out."

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:19.540
And then they call again, then I know a bit more.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:23.880
And sometimes on the basis of the factual information,

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:27.820
you already know whether you want to do it or not.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:33.620
You more easily know that you don't want to do it just by looking at the facts.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:38.040
Many people spend their lives in a state of

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:43.980
almost permanent dissatisfaction, unfortunately.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.640
So

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:51.220
they are maybe looking for some purpose, or they may have given up hope

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:57.140
that there 𝘪𝘴 some purpose for them, and they're just surviving or making a living.

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:58.520
(Oprah) Or caught up in the doing.

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:01.340
(Eckhart) Caught up in the doing, in the stress of it.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:01.920
- Right.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.040
- And so usually when we talk about purpose,

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:11.560
when people talk about purpose, they think of purpose in terms of future.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:14.560
"Where am I going, what am I supposed to do,

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:18.800
what's the direction I'm going in, what's my goal; the goal that I want to achieve?"

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:21.680
And that, of course, is there, it has its place.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:24.240
But I call that the outer purpose.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:29.380
More fundamental than the outer purpose is what most people usually overlook,

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:32.040
and that is the realization that

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:36.740
what matters most is finding your 𝘪𝘯𝘯𝘦𝘳 purpose.

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:42.540
So inner purpose is aligning your life fully

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:45.700
with the present moment.

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:49.860
So that you are no longer out of alignment with the present moment,

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:53.520
which leads to the state of dissatisfaction that we talked about

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:56.280
that is the reality for many people.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:12:00.780
So you have to go, first of all, beyond the state of dissatisfaction

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.760
that is so many peoples' reality.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:03.520
- Right.

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:06.740
- But you cannot go beyond the state of dissatisfaction

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:12.720
through some future goal that says, "One day, I would like to be in a state of fulfillment or satisfaction."

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:17.800
No. You have to enter the state of fulfillment and satisfaction

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:21.660
by becoming one internally with the present moment.

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:25.980
And your purpose-- and your 𝘪𝘯𝘯𝘦𝘳 purpose is

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:29.480
that alignment with where you are right now.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:33.780
To be totally where you are and whatever you are doing,

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:38.660
even if it doesn't look like you're- the life purpose that you want for the next 30 years.

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:44.180
Whatever you are doing now, to be total in doing it, no matter what it is.

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:48.240
To be true to life by being true to this moment.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:51.780
It's not that difficult

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:56.140
really, to step out of the stream of thinking.

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:59.840
To... one way, of course, is meditation.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.540
It's what the traditional approach is.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:06.660
You have certain periods of time, once or twice a day,

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:09.720
when you sit down, close your eyes,

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:16.140
and instead of involuntarily being drawn into the continuous stream of thinking,

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:20.980
you- usually with meditation, you have a technique or a  message-

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:26.660
you focus your attention on one thing, which could be a mantra that you repeat,

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:30.300
it could be your breathing,

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:34.480
it's a very ancient meditation. It could be the inner feeling in your body,

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:39.500
the sense of aliveness that pervades your body.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:43.060
In other words, you take attention away from thinking.

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:47.080
And that's already a great realization that you are able-

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:51.060
you actually have a choice of directing attention.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:55.740
You don't 𝘩𝘢𝘷𝘦 to go with your attention all the time

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:59.420
where the habitual thought patterns want you to go.

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:02.920
The habitual thought patterns 𝘸𝘢𝘯𝘵 your attention every time.

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:08.940
Every thought says, "[?] give me your attention, follow me. Go this way."

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:12.520
And another negative thought, and another one, and another one.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:17.800
Yes, compassion for yourself, of course it's as important as compassion for others.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.600
When...

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:23.660
Often, I get asked questions, like people who did something

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:28.440
that they now realize was deeply wrong in the past.

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.620
Sometimes people ask questions about-

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:36.440
they brought up their children in a way that they now realize was not very conscious,

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:40.220
and so they may have caused suffering to their children,

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:43.840
or other people find they have caused suffering to loved ones

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:46.880
and they now realize that what they did was wrong.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:49.880
And to gain- I say- this is an example

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:53.420
where you need to be compassionate with yourself,

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:58.580
because no human being can act beyond their level of consciousness,

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:01.440
so that was your level of consciousness at the time,

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:04.800
and you could not go beyond that.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:09.740
And again here, to make demands upon yourself,

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:13.280
up to a point, it might be a good thing to-

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:17.740
as long as you enjoy it, it's a wonderful thing.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:21.740
When the enjoyment of what you're doing is lost,

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:25.380
then you have to be careful. Because then you have to come to a stop and say,

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:27.880
"Okay, there's something here that's not right,

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:31.160
because I'm no longer enjoying what I'm doing."

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:34.880
A lot of so-called unhappiness

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:39.100
is also a childish way of trying to

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.300
change things

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:45.320
by being as unhappy as you can about them.

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:51.860
And the underlying unconscious or semi-conscious assumption is,

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:55.980
"If I'm really unhappy, somebody, perhaps God,

00:15:55.980 --> 00:16:00.540
is going to do something about it," or "I'm going to prove Him wrong,

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:04.120
I'm going to show Him how dreadful it is, and then finally-"

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:07.360
this is an unconscious assumption behind the unhappiness,

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:12.260
because you believe if you're habitually and frequently unhappy,

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:14.880
you believe that it has a purpose.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:20.400
It's an underlying assumption, perhaps you wouldn't verbalize it in that way,

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:23.540
but you believe that it works for you.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.720
Of course it doesn't, but

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:29.860
things are going to change, but just need to be really unhappy

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.520
so that God finally-- even if you don't believe in God,

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:39.680
this can still be the mechanism; the underlying unconscious assumption behind it.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:41.560
Something's going to happen.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:45.480
And of course, the opposite is true, because the more unhappy you are with something,

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:49.880
the more you're stuck in the situation. (chuckles)

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:53.520
How you do what you do is more important than what you do.

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:59.140
You could have a store serving customers with this or that,

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:04.400
which perhaps would not be regarded as a very important job,

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:08.300
and yet if that is done with a quality of presence

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:11.240
where every customer who comes into your store,

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:15.580
you give this person your-- just an example-- your fullest attention,

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:18.900
you appreciate him or her as a human being,

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:23.240
you see how you can best serve him or her in the present moment,

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:26.180
that is quality. And then you would be improving--

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:28.640
everybody who comes into contact with you

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:35.280
would somehow experience a small lifting in their being, in consciousness.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.440
And so that you could create-

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:41.220
even a person in a relatively simple job

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:44.660
could contribute in that way to creating a better world.

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:48.660
(Oprah reading)

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:03.440
(Eckhart) Yes. So what that means...

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:06.440
if nothing changes in your state of consciousness,

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:11.800
the ego has many ideas. It says, "I want to be a spiritual person."

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:15.520
"I want to be recognized as a spiritual person."

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:19.240
"I want to be more spiritual than all these people,

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:22.100
and I'm definitely more spiritual than 𝘺𝘰𝘶."

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:25.200
So the ego has all kinds of ideas of what it wants to be.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:28.400
It might even say, "Yes, I want to be good,"

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.180
because it wants to have a better image of itself.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:34.440
But on that level,

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:39.420
by the essential dysfunction of the ego is still operating.

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:44.960
So this is why we have the phrase, "the road to hell is paved with good intentions,"

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:47.660
because no matter how good your intentions are,

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:50.440
when you're still trapped in the ego,

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.480
it will always take you into conflict eventually.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.760
So you have to go deeper beyond the realm of opposites

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.620
where there's good and bad,

00:18:58.620 --> 00:19:04.700
and reach a place within yourself that is unconditioned,

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:08.940
that is, what I sometimes call, the formless.

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:13.860
Expressed beautifully in the Old Testament in the little saying,

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:17.940
"Be still and know that I am God."

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:20.540
That is- and that's in the Old Testament.

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:24.720
It contains the entire wisdom of religion

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.120
in those few words.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:29.920
Be still, meaning

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:34.960
go to that place where the mind is no longer operating,

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:39.720
where there's- you're just conscious without thinking,

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:44.780
and that is the level where the eternal resides.

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:48.860
Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:52.420
I made this video because LiveNow06 asked me to,

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:55.440
so if there's a famous entrepreneur that you want me to profile next,

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:57.540
leave in the comments below and I'll see what I can do.

